RustyRig installation for the LAN/VPN beta
========================================

Use doc/QUICKSTART.txt for station configuration, first login and receive-audio
checks. The following describes the current install paths; clean-machine
package installation and physical-radio acceptance still need release testing.

Debian packages
---------------
Build packages from a matching source/submodule checkout:

    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install jq fakeroot dpkg-dev debhelper
    ./install-deps.sh

Run the apt command it prints with sudo, then:

    make -j4 PROFILE=radio debs

Packages are written to the parent directory. Install only the packages you
need using sudo apt install with their explicit ./ paths. Shared-library and
DSP dependencies must come from the same release. Typical selections:

    rustyrig-server       Backend and station configuration
    rustyrig-client       Native terminal client
    rustyrig-client-gtk   GTK frontend, installed alongside the client
    rustyrig-fwdsp        GStreamer audio worker used by server/client

Optional packages include rustyrig-server-gpsd and callsign-lookup. Debug-symbol
and development packages are not needed for normal operation. apt resolves
GStreamer runtime dependencies; custom pipelines may require extra plugins.

A fresh server install asks for an admin password and initializes its database.
It also asks whether to enable the shared guest account, defaulting to No.
If enabled, its login is guest/guest, with the shipped guest radio/chat/TX
permissions subject to server restrictions and quotas.
Existing databases and modified configuration are preserved during upgrades.
Configure /etc/rustyrig/rrserver.cfg before starting:

    sudo systemctl enable --now rustyrig-server
    sudo journalctl -u rustyrig-server -f

The service runs as rustyrig, with /var/lib/rustyrig as its working directory.
Database: /var/lib/rustyrig/db/master.db.
Native config: /etc/rustyrig/rrclient.cfg.
Modules: /usr/lib/rustyrig/modules/rrserver and .../rrclient.
WebUI: /var/lib/rustyrig/www.
Grant the service account access to the specific audio/serial devices required
by your station. Keep code/module directories owned by root.

Source-tree runs and manual installation
---------------------------------------
You can run ./bin/rrserver and ./bin/rrclient without installing. The quickstart
lists the local database, module, DSP and WebUI path overrides required when
using copies of the packaged example configs.

make install copies binaries and libraries under INSTALL_DIR (default
/usr/local), configuration into CONF_DIR (default /etc/rustyrig), and WebUI
assets into WEB_ROOT (default /var/lib/rustyrig/www). It prompts before replacing
changed configuration files. It does not perform Debian's account/database
provisioning or service setup. For example, after building:

    sudo make PROFILE=radio install

Set path.modules to /usr/local/lib/rustyrig/modules/rrserver or .../rrclient,
and [fwdsp] path=/usr/local/bin/fwdsp when using that prefix. Ensure SQL template
and preload paths point to the repository's sql files or your installed copies,
and create writable database/runtime directories for the account running the
server. First database creation uses the random bootstrap-password flow described
in the quickstart.

Other distributions
-------------------
packaging/PKGBUILD and packaging/rustyrig.spec are starter Arch/RPM packaging.
See packaging/README.md for their current limitations and module layout.

Upgrades
--------
Back up configuration and the database using SQLite's backup facility before
upgrading. Preserve accounts, quota/audit history and your pipeline/device
settings. Upgrade server, libraries, native client and served WebUI together;
old wire-protocol compatibility is not provided. Check path.modules in existing
configs after upgrades, then repeat login, receive-audio and PTT-off checks.
